{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sam has only one measuring container. The volume of this container is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> cup. A recipe needs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dc3b842949e654670cb9beb13783085aa898d96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> cups of flour. How many times does Sam fill his <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> cup container to accurately measure the flour for this recipe?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22234ee6fdd37e81638a3c4896f7699f71a8f5cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 10 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4 \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"386\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8411f6d665f05414a2f51bbc6e1b2aca755134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2 \\times 2 + 1}{2} = \\frac{4 + 1}{2} = \\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"230\" height=\"38\" />, so Sam would fill the cup container <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31d561ee28c67fc22f4d306a38ea1d817b1bb17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{5}{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"95\" height=\"49\" /> times.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t